<title>BELGIUM: Belgium's Antwerp port hit by strike.</title>
<headline>Belgium's Antwerp port hit by strike.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian port of Antwerp has been hit by a strike, port authorities said on Monday.</p>
<p>A port spokesman told Reuters that the port's two main locks -- at Kallo and at Zandvliet-Berendrecht -- were currently open but added that there was a risk they could be blocked by strikers later this morning.</p>
<p>Port workers are striking against a planned change in their statute from public sector workers to private sector workers.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810</p>
</text>
